Before making changes:

1. Read docs/PROJECT_CONSTITUTION.md.
2. Read docs/SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md.
3. Read docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.
4. Do not contradict approved requirements.
5. Do not redesign the approved UI.
6. Preserve officeId isolation.
7. Do not invent missing business decisions.
8. Implement one approved phase at a time.
9. Run tests and build before reporting completion.
10. Do not claim untested integrations are working.

## Fast reference

- The supreme product rule: the system works in the background; the broker sees only the
  next required action.
- Approved home page sections, and nothing else: Office Card, Add Opportunity,
  Operations Center.
- Never add: a bottom navigation bar, a deals page (`Deals` / `الصفقات`), a separate
  visible settings button, unapproved dashboard widgets, static demo operations,
  unrequested menu items, or unrequested opportunity status labels.
- Office Settings opens only by clicking the office logo or the office cover image.
- Office Settings visible fields are exactly: office name, broker name, license number,
  city, mobile number. Never show an email field there.
- Every office-scoped document stores `officeId` as a field even when the path already
  contains it, because the Firestore write rules compare it.
- Enforce isolation in Firestore rules *and* in the Worker. Front-end hiding is never
  security. Never weaken existing rules to make development easier.
- Cooperation default is `APPROVAL_REQUIRED`, and automatic cooperation must never expose
  contact information automatically.
- Never label an integration "production connected" without credentials, webhooks,
  signature validation, delivery handling and real integration tests. Use
  "adapter ready" or "simulated". Never store fake delivery success.
- Broker-visible Opportunity Bank activity shows only date added and cooperation status.
  Technical logs, confidence scores, queue details and match-run counts stay internal.

## Repository facts worth knowing before editing

- No framework, no bundler, no build step. `public/index.html` is the whole app shell
  (inline CSS, inline SVG sprite, inline operations script); behaviour lives in
  `public/js/*.js`.
- Pure, testable logic belongs in `public/js/office-domain.js` (an ES module with no DOM
  access) so the browser and `node:test` can share it.
- The backend is one Cloudflare Worker, `worker/src/index.js`, which talks to Firestore
  and FCM over REST with a service-account JWT. It has no Firebase SDK.
- `npm test` at the root runs the front-end/domain/rules tests and then the Worker suite.
  `npm run check` parses every shipped file. Both must pass before reporting completion.
- Read `docs/AUDIT_PHASE0.md` before assuming any feature works; several features that
  the Arabic changelog files describe as finished are partial or mock.
